Package: energypal
Title: Energy-Focused Color Palettes for Data Visualization
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Date: 2026-08-03
URL: https://optimal2050.github.io/energypal/, https://github.com/optimal2050/energypal
BugReports: https://github.com/optimal2050/energypal/issues
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Oleg",
           family = "Lugovoy",
           email = "olugovoy@optimalsolution.dev",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5546-9875"))
Description: Curated colour palettes and source-matching functions for
    energy-related data visualisation. Palettes are specified as YAML files
    describing a hierarchy of energy carriers and technologies, alongside
    variants approximating the colour conventions of energy publications from
    the EIA, EPA, IPCC and Our World in Data, and continuous scales extracted
    from the Global Wind Atlas and Global Solar Atlas poster maps. A multi-stage
    matcher resolves the messy source labels found in real datasets to the
    canonical hierarchy, and 'ggplot2' scale functions apply the result to
    fuel-mix charts and other energy sector graphics. Each palette carries its
    own provenance and licence terms. Users can supply their own palette files.
